              selected
            </text>
            <text x="212" y="48" text-anchor="middle" class="limit-card-annotation">
              Trust anchor
            </text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Heuristic validation</h3>
        <p>
          Many certification path-building approaches rely on heuristic traversal strategies, local preferences, and early stopping conditions to find a valid certification chain.
        </p>
        <p>
          While effective in practice, these methods may fail to consistently discover all admissible paths or may depend on implementation-specific behavior to find a valid route at all.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="limit-card">
        <h3>Lack of trust governance</h3>
        <p>
          Trust is commonly inherited from hierarchies or broad anchors, rather than
          being selectively defined between issuing CAs and governed federation points.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="limit-card">
        <h3>No crypto agility awareness</h3>
        <p>
          Traditional federation models rarely score or prioritize paths according to
          classical, hybrid, and post-quantum cryptographic transitions, leaving
          crypto-agile interoperability under-specified.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

